# SPOKEDU MASTER — Product Governance

## Before any MASTER product work

Read at most these four:

1. [Product Constitution](../../docs/SPOKEDU_MASTER_PRODUCT_CONSTITUTION.md)
2. [Decision Protocol](../../docs/SPOKEDU_MASTER_PRODUCT_DECISION_PROTOCOL.md)
3. UI look: [Art Direction](../../app/spokedu-master/MASTER_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md)
4. If implementing: completed [Sprint Brief](../../docs/SPOKEDU_MASTER_SPRINT_BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md)

Surface audit, archived v3, and extra design essays are not implementation authority. See [Design Governance](../../docs/SPOKEDU_MASTER_DESIGN_GOVERNANCE.md).

## Authority (non-negotiable)

- **KEEP / explicit REFINE in brief** → may implement
- **REPLACE / REMOVE / new product semantics** → **Product Owner approval first**
- North Star or Constitution **does not** authorize silent contract changes

## Workflow

```
Audit (read-only) → Decision Gate → Sprint Brief → Implementation → Cross-check
```

Mid-implementation conflict → **STOP**, report, wait for approval.

## Runtime evidence

- Do **not** infer behavior from URL or component name alone
- Trace: callers, consumers, tests, state source, runtime transition, entitlement
- **Session route entry ≠ autostart** — verify `entry`, briefing, confirmation, engine state

## User segments

Distinguish first vs returning user; Free/Lite/Premium; Team/Center (sales-led, ≠ Premium); Admin (internal, ≠ customer plan).

## Scope discipline

- Do not implement product behavior **outside Sprint Brief**
- Do not expand scope for “improvement” or “unity” without approval
- Pair with **preserve-existing-behavior**: unrequested behavior change forbidden
- Pair with **work-principles**: pointer only — Visual SSOT owns look
- Pair with **cta-unity**: pointer only — Visual SSOT owns the six CTA kinds

## Rule conflicts

Do not pick arbitrarily. Report conflict; apply hierarchy in Constitution § Contract Hierarchy for **importance**, Decision Protocol for **change permission**.

## Verification

Respect **no-verify-shell**: no npm test/tsc/build unless user explicitly requests.

## Core principle

> **Think globally. Decide explicitly. Implement only approved scope.**

This rule is **not** permission to refactor broadly. It separates product thinking from implementation authority.
